usage: expectrail verify [-h] [--head HEAD] [--project PROJECT] [--base BASE]
                         [--adapter ADAPTER] [--game GAME] [--routes ROUTES]
                         [--specs SPECS] [--head-commit HEAD_COMMIT]
                         [--base-commit BASE_COMMIT]
                         [--execution-class {diagnostic,isolated}]
                         [--timeout TIMEOUT]
                         [--idempotency-key IDEMPOTENCY_KEY]
                         [--intent {fix,change,none}] [--bug TEXT|@FILE]
                         [--detach] [--json] [--auto-fix]
                         [--auto-fix-attempts N] [--auto-fix-usd-cap USD]
                         [--auto-fix-fixture PATCH | --auto-fix-recorded PATCH]
                         [--jobs-root JOBS_ROOT_AFTER]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --head HEAD           a checkout of the change
  --project PROJECT     the changed project folder; use its base config to
                        select routes, checks and vision
  --base BASE           a checkout of what it is compared with; the checks are
                        read from it
  --adapter ADAPTER
  --game GAME           the project folder, relative to the checkout
  --routes ROUTES       route files or globs, relative to the checkout,
                        separated by spaces or commas
  --specs SPECS         the folder of approved test specs, relative to the
                        checkout
  --head-commit HEAD_COMMIT
  --base-commit BASE_COMMIT
  --execution-class {diagnostic,isolated}
  --timeout TIMEOUT     seconds before the job stops as needs review
  --idempotency-key IDEMPOTENCY_KEY
  --intent {fix,change,none}
                        fix requires a check to fail on the base and pass on
                        the head three times each; change and none keep the
                        existing rule (default: none)
  --bug TEXT|@FILE      report with --intent fix; capture text or a UTF-8 file
                        (8192 characters max). Use @@ for a literal leading @.
                        No URL is fetched; this does not create a check
  --detach              start the job, print its id and return
  --json
  --auto-fix            try to repair a reject in a separate checkout
  --auto-fix-attempts N
                        1 to 10 attempts (default 3)
  --auto-fix-usd-cap USD
                        maximum Muse spend across attempts
  --auto-fix-fixture PATCH
                        use a fixture patch offline
  --auto-fix-recorded PATCH
                        replay a recorded patch offline
  --jobs-root JOBS_ROOT_AFTER
                        where jobs are kept (default: $EXPECTRAIL_JOBS, else
                        runs/jobs)
